# 00 — Technical PRD template

Canonical template: `docs/TEMPLATE_TECHNICAL_PRD.md`.
Copy it for every new feature or baseline slice PRD. Do **not** invent a parallel outline.

## Required document header (every PRD)

Immediately under the title, include this metadata table:

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Created | [Month Day, Year] |
| Version | 1.0 - Initial |
| Version Notes | [One-line summary] |

Example (`docs/authentication/SIMPLE_AUTH_PRD.md`):

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Created | January 19, 2026 |
| Version | 1.0 - Initial |
| Version Notes | Initial PRD for simple login/logout flow |

## Required sections (in order)

1. Overview/Problem
2. **Business Requirements — MANDATORY on every PRD** (feature and baseline). Never omit.
   Group under **named business-area headings** appropriate to the slice
   (auth example: **Authentication**, **Session Management**, **Logout**;
   owners example: **Find & View Owners**, **Register & Edit Owners**, **Owner Deletion**).
   Under each area: Users / Capabilities / Business rules (+ Current fulfilment for baselines).
3. Hypothesis (`We believe that [solution] will [outcome] for [user].`)
4. Scope (In Scope / Out of Scope / Cut)
5. Technical Requirements (Database Schema, API Endpoints, User Interface)
6. Implementation Phases (`COMPLETED` | `IN PROGRESS` | `PLANNED`)
7. Technical Implementation Details
8. Acceptance Criteria (checkboxes)
9. Success Metrics
10. Dependencies
11. Risks and Mitigation
12. Troubleshooting Guide
13. Notes for AI Agents
14. Current Status

Business Requirements = capabilities and rules **without** API routes or table names.
Technical Requirements owns schema, endpoints, and UI.

## When implementing from a PRD

1. Read Problem, Business Requirements, and Hypothesis first.
2. Honour Scope — do not build Out of Scope or Cut items.
3. Update phase status markers as work progresses.
4. **Document every final change in the appropriate PRD(s) before considering a phase done:**
   - Feature work → the feature PRD (e.g. `docs/authentication/SIMPLE_AUTH_PRD.md`)
   - Baseline facts that changed → the owning baseline PRD (e.g. `AUTHENTICATION_BASELINE_PRD.md`)
   - System-wide map → `ARCHITECTURE.md` when layer behaviour changes
   - Record: files touched, behaviour, test IDs, verification commands/results, troubleshooting
5. Record real implementation under Technical Implementation Details (cite `filepath:line-number`).
6. Check off Acceptance Criteria only when verified.
7. Add Troubleshooting entries when bugs are found and fixed.
8. Keep Current Status + Version / Version Notes current; drop outdated notes.
9. Bump **Version** / **Version Notes** in the header when the PRD meaningfully changes.

Layer conventions while coding: `01`…`07` rules. TDD: `07-tdd-workflow.mdc`.
